u please give me  the mortgage back and you'd be forced to  sell the house pay back the mortgage and  then they could blackmark you are you  going to go to prison for doing it no if  you've got a residential mortgage and  you've got a tenant in it should you be  losing sleep and  no but would i recommend doing that  absolutely i wouldn't recommend doing  that i understand what people do because  you're going to put down a very small  deposit and it's going to give you a  much higher return on investment but i  would really suggest that you get the  correct suitable mortgage and if i was  to say anything other than that i'd be  being a bad property advisor so  what's my opinion on it my opinion on it  is there's enough money in property  investment if you do it right to do it  properly  all right next ali baglam says  i want to get into property i'm 17 years  old i'm making 1  350 pounds per month through my job  what's your advice for the future  well if you're making 1  350 pounds a month  the first thing i'd say is you're  actually in a really good position  because i would rather be your mentor  than mentor somebody who's got a hundred  thousand pounds a year salary  but  they've got a wife and four kids and two  nice cars and a mortgage  and they need a hundred thousand pounds  to live  because  they're gonna need to create a hundred  thousand pounds  in property income  to cover their expenses  you're gonna need just over a thousand  pounds a month to cover your living  expenses so to replace your job for you  to become financially independent  is actually really really easy how would  i recommend doing it or for a start you  could rent an apartment  in your area  and then you could rent it out on airbnb  and booking.com and if you did that with  the correct contracts in place i mean  you're 17 years old so you might need to  do this um with with backing of somebody  but hey when i got started i was 17-2 i  got my first deal with 17. so you only  need to pull off one or two deals like  that where you don't even own the  property you just control them and you  can very comfortably replace your salary  so i think you're in a good place also  you've not probably got lots to lose  because you're only 17. i imagine that  you've not got  liabilities and big expenses over your  head so  i think the world is your oyster my  friend  danish iqbal says hi samuel i'm 17 years  old oh my goodness what is going on with  the 17 year olds great to have you on  the channel  i'm currently studying a levels which  take up my time however i want to become  a deal sourcer i've tried reaching out  to deal sources already regarding code  eagle sourcing but as i'm not compliant  however when they they ask me if i've  had had training or source deals before  i say no but when they realize they tend  to blank me what would you advise me to  do  so if you're looking to do codial  sourcing this is a very smart move this  is where you find deals and then you  just pass it to a deal sourcing company  and that deal sourcing company will sell  it for you they'll take care of the  contracts the investors the compliance  the selling the invoicing the terms and  conditions all that sort of stuff and  you'll get paid a percentage of that fee  um the reason they're asking you if  you've had training is probably because  they don't want you to bring them deals  and then the deals are rubbish  and they end up having to go that deal's  rubbish and you go why is it rubbish and  they go because blah blah blah blah and  they end up you become  a drain on their time and resources so  they want you to to be trained so that  you're finding great deals you've got  the knowledge you've got the experience  so that you're easy to deal with which  to be honest i think is  i understand why they do that  i mean you could offer to work for them  for free or maybe you could just get  trained and then you become more  valuable but i would do one or one or  the other make sure 