ck or if there's any boxes that are  not ticked in that's the most serious so  that was a little bit of a schoolboy  error i'm not going to lie  however  what should you do now well if you've  already bidded presumably you've paid a  deposit or have to pay a deposit so  you probably have to go ahead i'm not  sure what the terms are of the auction  it might be that it's not a massive deal  could you get  could you get uh planning permission to  split the titles without knowing the  details of the house i really couldn't  say  however if you'd like to have a  mentoring call with either myself or one  of my team where we can talk to you we  can talk to you about the ins and outs  of the house then you can book a free  mentoring call on the house we're not on  the house it's a pound  for seven day  trial of our unlimited mentoring through  samuel 365. i'll leave the details below  in the link which you can check out  all right last question samuel i want to  start property investing and i'm  currently  17 years old  what is going on but i'm worried about  not knowing all of the laws contracts  etc like article four basically all the  legal terms okay so sam  you don't know the terms  so however you're not probably at 17  you're probably not going to be buying  the property what i would do if i was  you is i would find properties and pass  them to investors for a finder's fee  ask investors what they're looking for  find the deals pass them on and charge  for your time  you will be getting paid to learn  your refining deals if you've missed  something  the investor will tell you that you've  missed it you'll be getting paid to  learn that's the best thing that you can  do  i hope you guys enjoyed this video don't  forget to comment your questions below  and i look forward to seeing you guys  next time  you

